{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04XB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V \\to W$", "MATH_0002": "$P$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$T \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nT \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\ar[d] &\nT \\times_\\mathcal{Y} V \\ar[d] \\ar[l] \\ar[r] &\nV \\ar[d] \\\\\nT & T \\times_\\mathcal{Y} W \\ar[l] \\ar[r] & W\n}\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{T \\times_\\mathcal{Y} V \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$P$", "MATH_0008": "$P$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-property-spaces-too}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:de53270c893e9923caf39489aba298d93bb0626fc489e9e74df5606d34988dfe", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5b99a6ea7fe8caddd4a6f9142aff2efc340baf2afa640d29c231a4067351c243", "source_text": "The implication from left to right follows from\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nAssume <MATH_0001> has <MATH_0002>. Let <MATH_0003> be a scheme, and let\n<MATH_0004> be a morphism. Consider the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0005>\nof algebraic spaces. The squares are cartesian.\nThe bottom left morphism is a surjective, flat morphism which is locally of\nfinite presentation, hence <MATH_0006> is an\nfppf covering. Hence the fact that the right vertical arrow has property\n<MATH_0007> implies that the left vertical arrow has property <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1799c21e3f549bf1e463a22dd1065844c85c36de4ec026c1c3f49e53318b9996", "unit_id": "tag:04XD:proof"}
